{"records":[{"id":"pntrtyfk7g","title":"DNA replication is highly resilient and persistent under the challenge of mild replication stress ","description":"Mitotic DNA synthesis (MiDAS) has been proposed to restart DNA synthesis during mitosis due to replication fork stalling in late interphase caused by mild replication stress (RS). Contrary to this proposal, we find that cells exposed to mild RS in fact maintain continued DNA replication throughout G2 and during G2-M transition in RAD51- and RAD52-dependent manners. Persistent DNA synthesis is necessary to resolve replication intermediates accumulated in G2 and disengage an ATR-imposed block to mitotic entry. Because of the continual nature, DNA synthesis at very late replication sites can overlap with chromosome condensation, generating the phenomenon of mitotic DNA synthesis. Unexpectedly, we find that the commonly-used CDK1 inhibitor, RO3306, interferes with replication to preclude detection of G2 DNA synthesis, leading to the impression of a mitosis-driven response. Our study reveals the importance of persistent DNA replication and checkpoint control to lessen the risk of severe genome under-replication under mild RS. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-04-14T14:37:00.767Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/pntrtyfk7g","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/pntrtyfk7g"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Chris","last_name":"Chan","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["DNA Replication","Cell Cycle Control","Mitosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zdb9ccrpm6","title":"Egger et al., Spatial organization and functions of Chk1 activation by TopBP1 biomolecular condensates, Cell reports (2024)","description":"Mendeley Data set containin all the raw data presented throughthout Egger et al., Cell reports (2024). \nEgger et al. implement their previously proposed ATR/Chk1 activation model by dissociating the functions of ATR and Chk1. Using reverse genetics and optogenetics, they show that Chk1 is phosphorylated at the interface of TopBP1 biomolecular condensates, triggering cell cycle checkpoints and slowing down replication fork progression.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-03-12T10:01:15.803Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zdb9ccrpm6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zdb9ccrpm6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Tom ","last_name":"EGGER","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jihane","last_name":"Basbous","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/00rbzpz17","name":"Agence Nationale de la Recherche","grant_id":"AAPG2021"},{"id":"http://dx.doi.org/10.13039/100016913","name":"MSDAVENIR","grant_id":null},{"id":"https://ror.org/00rbzpz17","name":"Agence Nationale de la Recherche","grant_id":"ANR-10-INBS-04"}],"categories":["Cell Biology","DNA Replication","DNA Damage Response"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"bsm3s864fv","title":"Miller et al 2023 \"p53 inhibitor iASPP is an unexpected suppressor of KRAS and inflammation driven pancreatic cancer\"","description":"Raw imaging data that was used to generate the figures for Miller et al 2023 \" p53 inhibitor iASPP is an unexpected suppressor of KRAS and inflammation driven pancreatic cancer\" . Please refer to the paper in Cell Death & Differentiation for more explanation.\nThe data discussed in Miller et al publication have been deposited in NCBI's Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO) and are accessible through GEO Series accession number GSE226595 (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE226595). Any additional information required to reanalyse the data reported in this paper is available from the lead contacts upon request..","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-04-06T20:04:26.963Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/bsm3s864fv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/bsm3s864fv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Lu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Paul","last_name":"Miller","orcid":"0000-0002-5800-1220"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Histology","Microscopy","Inflammation","Pancreatic Cancer","RNA Sequencing","Western Blot","Immunohistochemistry","Pancreatitis","P53","Fluorescence Activated Cell Sorting"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"789652xcr3","title":"PINK1/Parkin Influences Cell Cycle by Sequestering TBK1 at Damaged Mitochondria Inhibiting Mitosis","description":"This data is the western blot data for Sarraf, Sideris et al. \"PINK1/Parkin Influences Cell Cycle by Sequestering TBK1 at Damaged Mitochondria Inhibiting Mitosis”","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-08-04T17:55:40.736Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/789652xcr3","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/789652xcr3"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Alicia M.","last_name":"Pickrell","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ndvs5mf8hx","title":"CHK1 Inhibitor Blocks Phosphorylation of FAM122A and Promotes Replication Stress, Li et al.","description":"Set of raw data for Li et al., Mol Cell 2020","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-09-26T17:43:47.054Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ndvs5mf8hx","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ndvs5mf8hx"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Alan","last_name":"D'Andrea","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Mechanism of Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"gd4yfvryyh","title":"List of the transcripts differentially expressed in ATRA-resistant acute promyelocytic leukemia cells treated with the CHK1 inhibitor MK-8776, compared to untreated cells (Franza et al., 2023)","description":"The clinically relevant CHK1 inhibitor MK-8776 induces the degradation of the oncogenic protein PML-RARα and overcomes ATRA resistance in acute promyelocytic leukemia (APL) cells. Here we show the list of the 1055 transcripts that were found significantly differentially expressed in MK-8776-treated APL cells compared to untreated ones (FDR≤0.05; Benjamini–Hochberg correction). RNA samples have been amplified, fragmented, and labeled for array hybridization according to the manufacturer’s instruction. Samples were then hybridized ON, washed, stained, and scanned using the Affymetrix GeneChip Hybridization Oven 640, Fluidic Station 450 and Scanner 3000 7G (Thermo Fisher Scientific) to generate the raw data files. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-02-28T14:50:07.602Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/gd4yfvryyh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/gd4yfvryyh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Alessandra","last_name":"di Masi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Gene Expression","Transcriptomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"cf5vbhy67d","title":"Human SMARCA5 is continuously required for Nucleosome Spacing","description":"Western blot images from Figure 1A. The top half is an immunoblot with anti-SMARCA5 and anti-FLAG and the bottom half is an immunoblot with anti-GAPDH. On a PDVF membrane. Grayscale image of IR700 or IR800 channel via LICOR Odyssey. Precision plus blue protein ladder. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-12-13T07:31:14.955Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/cf5vbhy67d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/cf5vbhy67d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Monica","last_name":"Bomber","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"n656zp56cy","title":"Data for: Assessing the capacity, coverage and cost of 5G infrastructure strategies: Evidence from the Netherlands","description":"This processed data results from an analysis of the capacity, coverage and cost of different enhanced Mobile Broadband (eMBB) 5G infrastructure strategies for the Netherlands. The data represent both a supply-driven and demand-driven investment analysis. The supply-driven analysis estimates the capacity that can be provided to users via new spectrum, before network densification via small cells is required. The demand-driven analysis tests a range of required per user speeds including 30, 100 or 300 Mbps and quantifies the performance of strategies in meeting this demand. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-02-12T01:43:05.858Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/n656zp56cy","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/n656zp56cy"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Edward","last_name":"Oughton","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sietse","last_name":"van der Gaast","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Rudolf","last_name":"van der Berg","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Zoraida","last_name":"Frias","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Economics of Technology","Wireless Telecommunication Systems","5G"],"journal_issn":["07365853"]},{"id":"29w6jd6tvs","title":"Retinopathy of Prematurity Research Datasets on ROPDB","description":"Retinopathy of Prematurity (ROP) is a retinal disorder that may result in blindness in premature infants. Early detection and treatment of ROP can prevent vision loss. Ophthalmologists utilize an indirect ophthalmoscope as the primary technique for ROP screening. Two screening challenges include the scarcity of medical specialists and the inconsistency in ROP grading by various observers. Researchers utilize AI-driven ROP screening systems to assist medical professionals. One challenge in developing these systems is the absence of annotated datasets for fundus ima","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-07-09T09:24:32.368Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/29w6jd6tvs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/29w6jd6tvs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"nazar","last_name":"salih","orcid":"0000-0003-1977-9387"},{"first_name":"nebras","last_name":"hussein","orcid":"0000-0002-9812-0718"},{"first_name":"mohamed","last_name":"ksantini","orcid":"0000-0002-9928-8643"},{"first_name":"donia","last_name":"benhalima","orcid":"0000-0002-3893-6213"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Retinopathy of Prematurity","Health Care","Fundus Imaging","Deep Learning"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"6wyzgw8z8k","title":"The CST complex mediates end-protection at double-strand breaks and promotes PARP inhibitor sensitivity in BRCA1-deficient cells. DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2018.04.046","description":"Original data used for plotting the figures belonging to the study \"The CST complex mediates end-protection at double-strand breaks and promotes PARP inhibitor sensitivity in BRCA1-deficient cells\". ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-05-22T12:41:39.154Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/6wyzgw8z8k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/6wyzgw8z8k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Sven","last_name":"Rottenberg","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Marco","last_name":"Barazas","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer","DNA Repair","Olaparib","BRCA Gene"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":109099,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":123,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":109099,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":108740,"restricted":54,"embargoed":305},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":1715},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","cou